WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.750
This is very nice. That building is very nice, eh? It's beautiful

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:22.700
This looks like my studio. I've come
to MIT a number of occasions and I've

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:23.970
been mostly

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:29.450
fascinated by the participants or the students
I guess you would call them.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.520
These people are in a situation where
they have to find out

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.780
how to create the future.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.899
Little Sun is a way of holding hands

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:46.059
with the Sun. The project is about

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:50.589
our ability to take something which is
incredibly abstract like understanding

00:00:50.589 --> 00:00:51.210
energy

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:56.569
and then make it somehow tangible.

00:00:56.569 --> 00:00:59.829
It has a solar panel. It has batteries on the
inside

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:03.339
to store the energy and it has a small
LED to emit the energy as light. 

00:01:03.339 --> 00:01:07.570
There are 1.6
billion people in the world without

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:08.810
access to electricity

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:12.770
it's very much but energy poverty. It's
about lack of development opportunity.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:16.400
The work of art in my mind is not
necessarily this piece of plastic

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.340
it's much more the whole system of
working together with different entities

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.250
and people on the way taxes bring it to

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.910
finally rural users in a chain which will
ideally have

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.600
a number local profits in it on the way

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.150
When we had discussed bringing Little Sun

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.360
to MIT, it was because I have strong
confidence

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.410
in the sort of resonance between why and how

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:43.850
When people say something about how
they wanna do something

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:48.500
you can sometimes inside of that or
underneath that you can see why

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.049
Make it simple. Simplicity is crucial

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:54.430
The idea should like an elevator pitch

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:57.950
Hacking Arts is a festival and hackathon exploring the intersection of

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.090
art entertainment technology and
entrepreneurship

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:04.700
Little Sun is really such a perfect
example of the type of thing

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.900
That we want to encourage here. 

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.989
With the hackathon you get a chance to work on something, change it, see it in a different way

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.400
Little Sun is going to be really fun to hack on. 

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.340
What we're proposing is a community that centers around a website 

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.580
that's going to help the people who are involved in the

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.530
selling and distributing of Little Sun to do three things

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.560
To explore, to connect and to join 

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.480
There is a lot of
components about the project Little Sun

00:02:29.489 --> 00:02:34.040
which are very much about
social communities, infrastructure

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.970
The ability to

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.560
make choices for yourself, being
independent, saying

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.560
I'm gonna take the Sun and empower
myself and I'm gonna read

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.920
tonight. I'm going to educate myself.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.900
That could be a title

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.140
What? The Infinite Corridor, and it's taken, but

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.860
The Infinite Corridor... did I make that?

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.480
No that's their title for this space... because it's so long

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:58.980
Ah, the Corridor

00:02:58.980 --> 00:02:59.480
 

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:06.000
 

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:11.660
My work has tried to, in various ways
address this question of

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:16.450
is reality actually real? By being
real is it then relative and is it

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:19.120
construction? Could I change it? Could I
change my world?

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.120
Do what I do have an impact on my
surroundings?

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.490
Can I feel that impact or it just a
theoretical impact so

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:30.650
all those questions and if you think
about it Little Sun is right in there

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.220
in the heart of all these questions. 

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:39.520
What we are doing with Little Sun is we actually making a real impact for people in rural areas

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.200
We were curious about what visualizingthe

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.190
global community around Little Sun would look like

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.100
In looking at the globe with the pins sticking out

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:51.260
it brings awareness of
the collectivity of it

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:55.190
You need something in between theory and
action, which of course could be called 

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:55.810
MIT

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:56.750
(laughter)

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.160
Here the opportunities are immense

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:03.280
I mean the power of MIT's is far beyond the
power of any company that I know

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.450
and so I see that collaboration take
forming many many shapes

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:11.190
Electric circuits, material expertise

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:14.380
Is it battery expertise? Is it business
expertise?

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.530
I do think we need to start to

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:21.239
Treasure what creativity is capable of
now we're sort of

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:25.580
in an engineering environment. I really encourage and
suggest that you would reach out

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.210
and ask creative people. And that my slow
you down. It might take you on a detour

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:33.650
but generally speaking I really think
it's worth it

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:38.280
Creativity is the success of the
consequences that a choice

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:41.919
has. So T choose between red and blue but that
is not the creative choice

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:46.060
the creativity in the choice between red
and blue is the impact that this choice

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.919
has on the world

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:51.060
And you really only make these
creative

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.389
choices once you are inspired. See
now

00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:58.440
I would say that is a skill that one can
nurture

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.460
I think in the first idea has a lot of
potential

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.470
in, for instance off grid in building
community

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.479
Well thank you so much for... No thank you!

00:05:07.479 --> 00:05:12.139
A great amount of the success up MIT has
been its ability

00:05:12.139 --> 00:05:16.500
to lean out into other fields and I
would encourage this to continue

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.660
into the arts, into the dances, into the
writers and theaters and ballets and music

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:21.220
and so on

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:25.210
This is, I think, one of the solutions in
which we can create a lot of change

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:29.210
 

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:33.610
 

